/*!
** @mainpage leaf-framework
**
** leaf-framework is organized around a few public modules. Start with the
** module that matches the system you are integrating, then use the generated
** symbol pages as reference material when you need a specific type or function.
**
** @section modules Core Modules
**
** - @ref binary "Binary Serialization": portable binary writing, parsing,
**   version migration, and bounded reads.
** - @ref application "Application": application lifetime, scenes, RML UI, and
**   runtime statistics.
** - @ref modding "Modding": mod discovery, metadata, loading, localization, and
**   prototype registration.
**
** @section reference Reference Indexes
**
** The class, namespace, file, and member indexes remain available from the
** sidebar. They are secondary reference views rather than the intended starting
** point for learning the framework.
**
** @defgroup binary Binary Serialization
** @brief Portable binary writing, parsing, version migration, and bounded reads.
**
** @defgroup application Application
** @brief Application lifetime, scenes, RML UI integration, and runtime stats.
**
